1. Definitions

"Software" means this repository's source code, documentation, data,
models, generated artifacts, and any associated files, in any form.

"Academic Research Use" means use of the Software solely by (a) an
accredited degree-granting educational institution, or (b) an individual
acting in their personal capacity, in either case solely for
non-commercial teaching, academic publication, or scholarly research
purposes, where:
  (i) the results are not incorporated into a commercial product or
      service offered for sale, license, or paid use to any third party;
  (ii) the use is not performed under a government procurement contract,
      task order, prize challenge, or other agreement whose deliverables
      are intended for operational, production, or acquisition purposes;
      and
  (iii) the Software is not sublicensed, resold, or otherwise made
      available to a Commercial User or Government User except in
      unmodified academic publications describing the work.

"Commercial User" means any for-profit entity, or any person or entity
acting on behalf of a for-profit entity, that uses the Software for any
purpose other than Academic Research Use, including internal evaluation,
product development, or service delivery.

"Government User" means any national, federal, state, provincial,
tribal, local, or foreign government, any agency, department,
instrumentality, or military branch thereof, or any contractor or
subcontractor using the Software to perform work under a government
contract, grant, task order, or agreement, other than a grant whose sole
purpose is to fund Academic Research Use as defined above.

